---
/**
 * Widget lab: every configuration of the docs-widget illustrations that the three
 * documentation pages need, on one page, driven by exactly the config those pages
 * will use.
 *
 * WHAT IT IS FOR. Two things that are hard to do against the docs pages
 * themselves. First, seeing all the cases at once, in both themes and at every
 * breakpoint, without scrolling through reference documentation to find them.
 * Second, giving the drift test in tests/e2e/docs-widgets.spec.ts one URL where
 * every class name the components can render is guaranteed to be present, so the
 * test does not have to guess which docs page grew or lost a demo.
 *
 * STATUS: kept, as a permanent internal harness. It carries `noindex` and is
 * excluded from the sitemap by the `filter` on `sitemap()` in astro.config.mjs.
 * Those two go together: a crawler that never fetches the page cannot read the
 * meta tag, so dropping either one leaves the URL indexable. If this page is ever
 * renamed or retired, update the filter in the same commit, and repoint the drift
 * test in tests/e2e/docs-widgets.spec.ts, which relies on this URL rendering
 * every class name the components can produce.
 *
 * The `state` readouts under each demo are the harness, not the component. They
 * exist so an interaction can be checked without opening devtools, and so the
 * change event contract is visible.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocsWidgets from '../components/docs-widgets/DocsWidgets.astro';

/* Configs are the real thing, not paraphrases: each of these objects is what the
   corresponding docs page passes to the widget today, so if the demo and the code
   sample above it ever disagree, it shows up here first. */
